</figure>
<div id="S7.SS3.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS3.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">On Stable Diffusion XL, as shown in Tab. <a href="#S7.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ 7.3.3 Stable Diffusion XL ‣ 7.3 More Experimental Results ‣ 7 Experiments Details ‣ LESA: Learnable Stage-Aware Predictors for Diffusion Model Acceleration" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, <span id="S7.SS3.SSS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">LESA</span> consistently delivers better visual quality than DeepCache across all acceleration levels <math id="S7.SS3.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}</annotation></semantics></math> from 3 to 10, with higher ImageReward and CLIP scores, higher PSNR and SSIM, and lower LPIPS. Compared to DeepCache at <math id="S7.SS3.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}{=}10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}{=}10</annotation></semantics></math>, <span id="S7.SS3.SSS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">LESA</span> increases ImageReward from -0.01 to 0.22 and CLIP score from 31.81 to 32.56, while PSNR rises from 28.29dB to 28.94dB and LPIPS drops from 0.51 to 0.43.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S7.T8" class="ltx_table">

