<p id="S7.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:70%;">Note:</span><span id="S7.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;"> All methods inherit baseline memory optimizations (e.g., FlashAttention). ToCa is incompatible with these, hence its higher reported cache usage. </span><span id="S7.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:70%;">Actual cache memory usage</span><span id="S7.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;"> for each method should be computed as: </span><span id="S7.I1.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;">Peak VRAM during inference <math id="S7.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>−</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-</annotation></semantics></math> Baseline VRAM before inference</span><span id="S7.I1.i1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">.</span></p>
